     "text": [
      "Artificial Intelligence (AI) is like a super-smart computer that can think and learn like a human being. It's a technology that helps machines make decisions, understand data, and perform tasks on their own, without being explicitly programmed.\n",
      "\n",
      "Imagine you have a personal assistant, like Siri or Alexa. They can answer your questions, set reminders, and even understand your voice commands. That's because they're using AI to recognize and respond to your inputs.\n",
      "\n",
      "AI works by using algorithms, which are like recipes for computers to follow. These algorithms are designed to analyze data, identify patterns, and make predictions or decisions. This process is called machine learning.\n",
      "\n",
      "There are different types of AI, including:\n",
      "\n",
      "1. Narrow AI: This is like a super-smart robot that can perform a specific task, like recognizing faces or playing chess.\n",
      "2. General AI: This is like a super-smart human that can do anything, solve any problem, and understand any task.\n",
      "3. Superintelligence: This is like a super-smart AI that's way beyond what humans can do.\n",
      "\n",
      "The goal of AI is to create machines that can think, learn, and act like humans, making our lives easier, more efficient, and more enjoyable.\n",
      "\n",
      "Some examples of AI in everyday life include:\n",
      "\n",
      "* Image recognition on your phone or computer\n",
      "* Personalized recommendations on streaming services\n",
      "* Self-driving cars and drones\n",
      "* Chatbots and virtual assistants\n",
      "\n",
      "Overall, AI is a powerful technology that's changing the way we live, work, and interact with machines.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from ollama import chat\n",
    "\n",
    "response = chat(\n",
    "    model=\"llama3.2\",\n",
    "    messages=[\n",
    "        {\n",
    "            \"role\": \"user\",\n",
    "            \"content\": \"Explain Artificial Intelligence in simple words.\"\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    ]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(response.message.content)\n"
   ]
  }
